--TEST--
A `use`, `autoload`, `type` or `namespace` written inside a body is `E0233`, never a panic — `rule:classes/a-type-is-declared-at-file-scope`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// A declaration is in effect before any code runs, so a body is the one place
// it has no reading at all.
class Outer {
    public static function run(): int {
        use App\Thing;
        autoload 'App' from './src';
        return 1;
    }
}
// A block at file scope is not file scope.
if (true) {
    type Handle = int;
}
// An anonymous function body is a body like any other. The statement form is the only one
// — `namespace Inner { … }` is `E0243` wherever it is written — so what this
// asks about is the position, not the spelling.
callable $f = fn (): int => {
    namespace Inner;
    return 1;
};
echo "unreached\n";
--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0233]: a nested `use` declaration is not supported
  --> %s:6:13
  |
6 |         use App\Thing;
  |             ^^^^^^^^^ this `use` would only take effect once control reached this statement
  = help: move the `use` to the top level of the file, above the code that needs it. It applies to the code below it

error[E0233]: a nested `autoload` declaration is not supported
  --> %s:7:9
  |
7 |         autoload 'App' from './src';
  |         ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ this `autoload` would only take effect once control reached this statement
  = help: move the `autoload` to the top level of the file, above the code that needs it. It applies to the code below it

error[E0233]: a nested `type` declaration is not supported
   --> %s:13:10
   |
13 |     type Handle = int;
   |          ^^^^^^ `Handle` would only exist once control reached this statement
   = help: move `Handle` out to file scope — every type in Novis is declared before any code runs, so a name's existence never depends on control flow

error[E0233]: a nested `namespace` declaration is not supported
   --> %s:19:15
   |
19 |     namespace Inner;
   |               ^^^^^ this `namespace` would only take effect once control reached this statement
   = help: move the `namespace` to the top level of the file, above the code that needs it. It applies to the code below it

error: aborting due to 4 errors
